          "distinct": false,
          "id": "351018233605bee21e0a8adca65c9594614009f9",
          "message": "chore(ci): restore nightly Linux idle benchmarks and surface failures (#4920)\n\n# Chore Summary\n\n<!-- Briefly describe the maintenance work in this PR. -->\n\nThe Linux idle benchmark was already scheduled, but the engine never\nstarted: the suite referenced `otlp-attr-otlp-idle.yaml` instead of\n`otlp-attr-otlp-idle.yaml.j2`. The [November 23 nightly\nrun](https://github.com/open-telemetry/otel-arrow/actions/runs/45212784180/job/137825750981#step:24:1)\nreported success because `tee` masked the script's exit status, and\nneither idle artifact was uploaded.\n\nThis change corrects the template path, runs the idle step with Bash's\n`pipefail`, and fails each idle artifact upload if it finds no files. It\nalso links the existing [Idle\nState](https://open-telemetry.github.io/otel-arrow/benchmarks/nightly/idle-state/)\nand [Idle Memory\nScaling](https://open-telemetry.github.io/otel-arrow/benchmarks/nightly/idle-memory-scaling/)\ncharts from the benchmark README. It does not change the schedule,\nworkload, or reported metrics. The [nightly category\nlist](https://github.com/open-telemetry/otel-arrow/blob/benchmarks/docs/benchmarks/nightly/index.html)\nis maintained on the `benchmarks` branch.\n\n## Related issue\n\n<!-- Link the related issue if one exists. -->\n\nNone linked.\n\nSigned-off-by: Utkarsh Umesan Pillai <utpilla@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Utkarsh Umesan Pillai <utpilla@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>",
